Package: halcyon
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINT@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= @LIBC@), python3 (>= 3.10), python3-numpy, python3-scipy
Recommends: hamlib-utils
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Description: open HF data modem (OFDM + LDPC, 2.75 kHz)
 Halcyon is an open high-frequency data modem: OFDM with LDPC coding and
 adaptive speed levels spanning 10 bit/s to about 8 kbit/s, all inside the
 2.8 kHz bandwidth that FCC 47 CFR 97.307(f)(3) allows on the amateur bands.
 .
 It brings a browser console for the waterfall, speed ladder and transcript;
 a host-mode TCP service so PAT, Winlink Express and VarAC can attach; clients
 for a Hermes Lite 2 and for TCI radios; and full CAT control of any rig that
 Hamlib's rigctld drives.
 .
 The package also installs halcyon-modem, a C++17 implementation of the modem
 core that decodes a 384 ms burst in about 45 ms.
